---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import avatar from "../assets/avatar.jpg";

const url = new URL(Astro.url);
const avatarParameter = url.searchParams.get("avatar");
---

<div
  class="max-w-3xl mx-auto sm:my-10 bg-white px-5 py-8 sm:p-8 sm:rounded-lg text-base sm:text-sm max-sm:leading-relaxed"
>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-8 gap-4">
    <div class="col-span-8 sm:col-span-6">
      <section>
        <div class="text-2xl font-semibold">Stas Strugovshchikov</div>
        <div class="text-base">
          Software Engineer | Solutions Architect | 10+ years of experience
        </div>
        <div class="mt-2">
          Orlando, Florida, 🇺🇸 USA · Open to relocation
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-3">
        <p class="mt-1">📞 +1 (786) 325 4891</p>
        <p class="mt-1">✉️ stanislav.stru@gmail.com</p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 divide-x divide-gray-500 mt-1">
          <span class="pr-3">
            🔗 <a
              href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/strugovshchikov"
              target="_blank"
              class="text-blue-600">LinkedIn</a
            >
          </span>
          <span>
            🔗 <a
              href="https://github.com/stanislavstru"
              target="_blank"
              class="text-blue-600">GitHub</a
            >
          </span>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    {
      avatarParameter && (
        <div class="col-span-8 sm:col-span-2 order-first sm:order-none">
          <Image
            src={avatar}
            alt="Stanislav Strugovshchikov"
            class="rounded-lg w-24 sm:w-auto"
          />
        </div>
      )
    }
  </div>

  <section class="mt-6 sm:mt-5">
    <p>
      Full Stack Engineer with 10+ years of experience building web and mobile
      products end to end, from React and Next.js frontends to Python (FastAPI),
      Node.js and PHP backends. Currently working on a cross-platform React
      Native app with a focus on real-device performance: profiling, list
      virtualization and smooth navigation on low-end Android. Hands-on with AI
      in production: integrated GPT content generation with deduplication,
      built LLM-driven marketing tools at a Y Combinator-backed startup, and
      trained custom models. Strong in multi-user system architecture,
      including role-based access and OAuth. Delivered projects for marketing
      platforms, banks, streaming services and e-commerce. I build products
      that are fast, scalable and genuinely easy to use.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 sm:mt-4">
    <h2 class="font-semibold text-xl">Skills</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc ml-5 sm:ml-6 mt-1 space-y-1.5 sm:space-y-0">
      <li>
        <strong>Languages:</strong> TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, PHP, HTML, CSS
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Frontend:</strong> React, Next.js, Redux, Redux-Saga, React Query,
        SWR, Tailwind CSS, Storybook etc.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Mobile:</strong> React Native, Ionic
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Backend:</strong> Node.js, FastAPI, Django, Laravel, Symfony, Yii2,
        Moleculer, WebSockets, Socket.IO, Drizzle ORM, io-ts, etc.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Databases:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, Redis
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI / LLM:</strong> OpenAI API (GPT-4/5), Anthropic Claude API, Meta
        Llama (self-hosted, fine-tuning), Hugging Face, Ollama, vLLM, LLM content
        generation pipelines, deduplication, custom model training
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Architecture & Security:</strong> Microservices, Monorepo, REST API,
        GraphQL, OAuth 2.0, JWT, Iron Session, Role-based access control
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Testing:</strong> Jest, Cypress, Playwright
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>DevOps & Infrastructure:</strong> Terraform, Infrastructure as Code
        (IaC), Docker, AWS (S3), Google Cloud Platform (GCP), Vercel, Firebase,
        CI/CD, Git, Webpack, Babel, ESLint, Prettier
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Design:</strong> Figma, Responsive layout, UI/UX
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 sm:mt-4">
    <h2 class="font-semibold text-xl">Experience</h2>

    <div class="sm:ml-3 mt-1">
      <div class="mt-2">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">
          Full Stack Engineer, Software Architect
        </h3>
        <a class="inline-block" href="https://www.ivigee.com/" target="_blank"
          ><h3 class="text-md font-bold">iVigee</h3></a
        >
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          July 2025 – Present · Burlington, Massachusetts
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1">Biotechnology Research.</p>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 sm:ml-6 mt-2 space-y-1.5 sm:space-y-0">
          <li>
            Designed the application architecture for handling sensitive
            biotech data, with role-based access control, secure authentication
            and strict data isolation.
          </li>
          <li>
            Built the team's AI-assisted development workflow end to end: UI
            generation from Figma designs via MCP, governed by a documented
            system of AI skills and rules that describes every process in the
            application.
          </li>
          <li>
            Set up a multi-stage code quality pipeline with strict linting, type
            checking and automated checks at every step, from local commits to
            CI.
          </li>
          <li>
            Mentored engineers and led code reviews, owning PR review standards
            across the team.
          </li>
          <li>
            Designed a scalable frontend architecture with TypeScript and a
            modular component structure.
          </li>
          <li>
            Optimized performance with server-side rendering (SSR) and dynamic
            rendering strategies.
          </li>
          <li>
            Built the API layer and data fetching strategy with controlled
            caching.
          </li>
          <li>
            Partnered with backend and business teams to deliver secure internal
            tools for biotech research.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 sm:mt-4">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Software Architect (Pet project)</h3>
        <a class="inline-block" href="https://copyext.com/" target="_blank"
          ><h3 class="text-md font-bold">NeptoLab</h3></a
        >
        <p class="text-gray-600">February 2025 – March 2026 · Tampa, Florida</p>
        <p class="mt-1">
          AI Content Generation Platform. Primary contributor (100+ commits) to
          an AI-powered content creation and publishing platform.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 sm:ml-6 mt-2 space-y-1.5 sm:space-y-0">
          <li>
            Built an AI content-generation system on GPT-4/5 with image
            generation, trend extraction and duplicate-content detection.
          </li>
          <li>
            Integrated publishing to Telegram, LinkedIn, WordPress and other
            with scheduling and queue processing on cron and Supabase Edge
          </li>
          <li>
            Architected a cross-platform mobile app from scratch (React Native,
            Expo, TypeScript) as a Turborepo/pnpm monorepo with a shared UI kit
            and a typed API client generated from the backend OpenAPI spec;
            authored 90%+ of commits.
          </li>
          <li>
            Built the mobile data layer: TanStack Query with tiered caching and
            offline support, single-flight token refresh, idempotency keys,
            secure token storage, and forms on React Hook Form + Zod.
          </li>
          <li>
            Delivered core flows: SMS sign-in, multi-step sign-up, onboarding,
            feeds, post with photo cropping, profiles and invite deep links.
          </li>
          <li>
            Built a design system from Figma via Figma MCP: design tokens, 14
            components and 120+ icons, documented in Storybook.
          </li>
          <li>
            Provisioned production infrastructure with Terraform/OpenTofu:
            managed Kubernetes with autoscaling, PostgreSQL replicated across 3
            availability zones, Redis/Valkey, Kafka (KRaft), OpenSearch and
            S3-compatible storage.
          </li>
          <li>
            Secured the platform with private-network-only data stores,
            Terraform-generated secrets in a cloud secrets manager,
            least-privilege IAM, SSO (OIDC + oauth2-proxy) and RBAC-limited CI
            access.
          </li>
          <li>
            Deployed services with Helm, Kustomize and GitLab CI; cut
            infrastructure costs by consolidating services behind a shared load
            balancer.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 sm:mt-4">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">
          Full Stack Engineer, Software Architect
        </h3>
        <a class="inline-block" href="https://www.criya.co/" target="_blank"
          ><h3 class="text-md font-bold">Criya</h3></a
        >
        <p class="text-gray-600">June 2022 – May 2025 · San Jose, California</p>
        <p class="mt-1">
          Criya AI, Y Combinator and venture backed AI startup is an intelligent
          content system.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 sm:ml-6 mt-2 space-y-1.5 sm:space-y-0">
          <li>
            Designed application architecture from scratch. Migrated Ruby app to
            Next.js - improved performance & SEO.
          </li>
          <li>
            Integrated LLM-based workflows for AI-driven marketing. Enabled users
            to generate content based on existing companies through a
            step-by-step questionnaire system and a knowledge base capable of
            storing virtually any type of data.
          </li>
          <li>
            Championed AI adoption, making Criya one of the first YC startups to
            deploy large-scale LLM workflows in production.
          </li>
          <li>Developed a custom page builder with a user-friendly structure.</li>
          <li>
            Integrated numerous third-party services (payments, analytics,
            auth), ensuring scalability and reliability.
          </li>
          <li>
            Built NX monorepo architecture, reducing build times by 50% and
            simplifying collaboration across teams.
          </li>
          <li>
            Developed a style library based on pure React components and
            Tailwind CSS.
          </li>
          <li>
            Developed cross-platform React Native app for quick content
            creation.
          </li>
          <li>
            Provided mentorship and technical leadership to junior developers.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 sm:mt-4">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">
          Lead Frontend Engineer, Software Architect
        </h3>
        <a class="inline-block" href="https://dzsystems.ru/en/" target="_blank"
          ><h3 class="text-md font-bold">DZ Systems</h3></a
        >
        <p class="text-gray-600">April 2017 – June 2022</p>
        <p class="mt-1">
          Leading IT services provider delivering scalable web platforms and
          digital transformation solutions across multiple industries. Worked
          across several high-impact projects in roles ranging from Frontend
          Engineer to Software Architect.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-5 sm:ml-6 mt-2 space-y-1.5 sm:space-y-0">
          <li>
            Built a professional social network with a chat system, cutting
            global negotiation steps from 5 to 3.
          </li>
          <li>
            Led architectural decisions and code reviews, ensuring clean,
            maintainable, and scalable solutions
          </li>
          <li>Migrated legacy projects from jQuery to Next.js.</li>
          <li>
            Created standardized collaboration guidelines, which standardized
            processes and guidelines, resulting in 3 times increase in
            development speed. Introduced modern CSS frameworks to enhance
            styling and maintainability.
          </li>
          <li>
            Optimized PostgreSQL database performance by 37% without changing
            the number of queried parameters.
          </li>
          <li>
            Drove modernization of the tech stack, transforming legacy products
            into high-performance applications
          </li>
          <li>
            Played a key role in scaling the platform to support 147 shops,
            managing both frontend and backend complexity. Used Yii2.
          </li>
          <li>
            Our team worked on SEO optimization, resulting in over 43% of our
            websites ranking in the top 1-3 positions.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 sm:mt-4">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">
          Full-Stack Engineer, Software Architect
